    {
      "title": "Produce and submit the maximal trial",
      "explanation": "Let $g$ be the surrogate gradient and $A$ the average-KL Hessian at the old parameters. Conjugate gradient approximately solves $As=g$, producing the persistent direction $s_{\\mathrm{dir}}$. The solver forms $\\theta_{\\mathrm{prop}}=\\theta_{\\mathrm{old}}+\\beta_{\\max}s_{\\mathrm{dir}}$, where $\\beta_{\\max}=\\sqrt{2\\delta/(s_{\\mathrm{dir}}^TAs_{\\mathrm{dir}})}$, then submits that trial to line search before either nonlinear check.",
      "sourceIds": [
