    {
      "title": "Submit and check a shorter trial",
      "explanation": "Backtracking shrinks $\\beta$ while preserving $s_{\\mathrm{dir}}$, so $\\theta_{\\mathrm{try}}=\\theta_{\\mathrm{old}}+\\beta_{\\mathrm{try}}s_{\\mathrm{dir}}$ lies on the same direction as $\\theta_{\\mathrm{prop}}$. The shorter trial is submitted before reevaluation. In this symbolic example, the resulting values satisfy $L_{\\mathrm{try}}>L(\\theta_{\\mathrm{old}})$ and $D_{\\mathrm{try}}\\le\\delta$; these are illustrative assumptions, not measurements.",
